1500 BM$="David: ARGH! A needle is piercing my heart!!":GOSUB 5100
1510 BM$="David was writhing in pain.":GOSUB 5100
1520 BM$="Susanna: David, what's wrong?! Does your chest... Ah! It must be the King of\the North!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1530 BM$="Devil King: What?! The King of the North?! Curses! He struck while David's\consciousness was in control... He might actually kill him!":GOSUB 5100
1540 BM$="Devil King: Urgh! My blood...?! David's blood, roused by the pain, is taking\over my blood! Am I going to be defeated by the King of the North?!":GOSUB 5100
1550 BM$="Devil King: Susanna! You must cast a defensive barrier! If you will not,\David's blood will boil and burst out of this body!":GOSUB 5100
1560 BM$="Seeing David suffering, Susanna had no choice but to obey. She left to\gather the tools she needed to create the barrier.":GOSUB 5100
1570 BM$="When she returned, she was not sure whether she should actually proceed\or not. What was the point of saving David from the King of the North, only\for his mind to be destroyed by the Devil King...?":GOSUB 5100
1580 BM$="Devil King: What are you doing, Susanna?! Are you going to stand there and\watch David suffer?!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1590 BM$="Susanna: Even if I cast the barrier, he's going to lose his mind forever. I\wouldn't be saving him - I'd just be exchanging one death for another!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1600 BM$="Devil King: Are you saying it is better for him to go through this torture?\Without his consciousness, he will no longer feel anything, including pain. If\you truly love him, then cast the barrier and spare him the agony!":GOSUB 5100
1610 GOSUB 6140:BM$="In tears, Susanna drew a magic circle, and started chanting her spell.":GOSUB 5100
1620 BM$="Devil King: Cease that pathetic whining! You must devote mind and body to\the spell if you wish to spare David from his torment!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1630 BM$="Seeing David squirm in pain, Susanna focused her mind on the spell. Finally,\his expression relaxed.":GOSUB 5100
1640 GOSUB 9090:GOSUB 6130:BM$="David: The pain is leaving... It must be your barrier... Thanks, Susanna... and\goodbye...":GOSUB 5100
1650 BM$="David: Devil King! If you want my body, hurry up and take it! At this rate,\Susanna's going to die!":GOSUB 5100
1660 COMMON FO:POLL X:ISET X:BM$="David's blood went still, and the blood of the Devil King was replacing it\once more. David's consciousness began to fade... He seemed to have\accepted his fate.":GOSUB 5100
1665 GOSUB 9020:'
1670 W2=0:GOSUB 6110:GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: David, don't go! What am I going to do without you?!":GOSUB 5100
1680 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Devil King: ...David is no more. His memories are gone. I no longer require the\barrier. David has truly become the Devil King.":GOSUB 5100
1690 BM$="Devil King: Susanna, I forgive you for breaking the dark laws. In return, you\must serve as my personal slave. Forever.":GOSUB 5100
1700 BM$="Susanna's eyes were no longer looking at David. They were looking at\someone who used to be David.":GOSUB 5100
1710 BM$="Devil King: Pour the blood of the dead northern tribesman onto a plate! I\shall reverse the flow of the spell of the King of the North. He will feel the\agony of his own magic!":GOSUB 5100
1720 GOSUB 6150:BM$="Without a word, Susanna obeyed the Devil King's order. She poured the\blood of the corpse into a plate.":GOSUB 5100
1730 BM$="Devil King: You should be ashamed to call yourself a dark sorceress with\your meager knowledge of magic. Observe, Susanna. This is how you cast\the dark spell reversal.":GOSUB 5100
1740 GOSUB 7000:GOSUB 6160:BM$="David, the Devil King, chanted a spell. Then, he threw the bloody plate\South.":GOSUB 5100
1745 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 9545:GOSUB 6170:BM$="The stone wall, hit by the plate, was stained crimson with blood.":GOSUB 5100
1750 GOSUB 6180:BM$="Then, blood started pouring from the wall.":GOSUB 5100
1755 GOSUB 6190:BM$="It poured copiously, as if the stone wall itself was alive... Could that have\been the blood of the King of the North?":GOSUB 5100
1760 GOSUB 9090:GOSUB 6200:BM$="Devil King: The blood of the King of the North has been severed... How\pathetic, to expire from a mere spell reversal. Perhaps time has diluted\his bloodline, weakening his magic. I suppose the same has happened to all":GOSUB 5100:BM$="sorcerers, dark and northern alike.":GOSUB 5100
1770 GOSUB 6110:W3=0:GOSUB 6320:BM$="Devil King: Susanna, send a summon to all sorcerers in the world! I shall\establish a Dark Kingdom. Any country that will not submit shall be\annihilated with my forbidden arts!":GOSUB 5100
1780 BM$="Devil King: Rejoice, Susanna! Your beloved David will become the king of\the world!":GOSUB 5100
1790 GOSUB 9080:GOSUB 6210:BM$="Susanna was not listening to the Devil King. She approached the man that\used to be David... and hurled herself at him, piercing his heart with a\dagger she had been hiding.":GOSUB 5100
1800 GOSUB 9526:BM$="Susanna: The blood of the King of the North has been severed... I won't let\you disgrace David's body any longer! Brand me as a traitor if you want!\I don't fear your punishment!":GOSUB 5100
1810 GOSUB 6260:BM$="The Devil King, his chest pierced, slowly pointed a finger towards Susanna.":GOSUB 5100
1820 GOSUB 9070:GOSUB 6220:BM$="She screamed, as blood started oozing out of her body. She collapsed,\squirming in a pool of her own blood.":GOSUB 5100
1830 GOSUB 9090:GOSUB 6230:BM$="She did her best to resist the urge of crying in pain. She did not want to\give the Devil King that satisfaction. Now, she could only await death...":GOSUB 5100
1840 POLL X:COMMON FO:GOSUB 6240:BM$="Shortly after, David's body collapsed, falling onto Susanna's blood.\Agonizing, she crawled towards him.":GOSUB 5100
1850 GOSUB 9010:BM$="As death was upon them, they managed to grab each other's hand.":GOSUB 5100
1860 BM$="As their consciousness faded, they had forgotten their pain. They left\this world together, smiling...":GOSUB 5100
1870 GOSUB 6250:BM$="The next day, a large crowd had gathered at St. Radford's Church in\Stratford, south of the castle where these events have occurred. They\were mourning the death of Archbishop Mellis.":GOSUB 5100
